# Utility Factory — environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you have.
#
# Supabase is the normal path: it provides authentication and durable storage.
# With no variables set the app still runs, but in local demo mode against an
# in-memory store seeded with clearly-marked demo data that resets whenever the
# server restarts. That mode is for trying the product out, not for running it.

# --- Supabase (persistence + authentication) --------------------------------
# Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard. Both are required; setting
# them is what switches the app out of demo mode.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- DataForSEO (keyword metrics + SERP) ------------------------------------
# API credentials from https://app.dataforseo.com/api-access — these are the
# API login and password shown there, NOT your dashboard account password.
# Enables the Research screen, "Refresh from provider" on an opportunity, and
# "Fetch top 10" on the SERP tab. Select DataForSEO under Settings -> Providers
# once these are set. Live calls consume DataForSEO credits.
DATAFORSEO_LOGIN=
DATAFORSEO_PASSWORD=

# --- AI provider ------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables the "Analyze opportunity" action. Without it the AI tab shows a
# configuration state and no analysis is ever fabricated.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional model override. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# --- Not yet implemented ----------------------------------------------------
# Search Console comes after the first real utilities are published and indexed,
# since there is nothing to measure until then. Asset metrics stay manual until
# then. Add an adapter under src/lib/providers/ and register it in
# src/lib/providers/registry.ts.
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
